## Context
2026-10-15, host doudou: `python3 scripts/zotero.py reconcile .` in report mode
on the harness, with a library index cache older than 24 h
(`~/.cache/zotero-import/index-95318.json`, 4.7 MB, written 2026-10-14 15:21),
was killed by `timeout 300` with no report and the cache unchanged. The time
went into `load_index` → `build_index` (Web API rebuild); cause not yet
established — slow paging, rate limiting (Backoff/Retry-After), or a request
without a timeout are candidates. Any real `/zotero reconcile`, `audit` or
import on a stale cache pays this cost.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] One timed rebuild with per-request logging identifies where the time goes
- [ ] Rebuild is incremental (`since=<library version>`) or bounded, and every HTTP call has a timeout
- [ ] A rebuild that cannot finish reports `unchecked` within a stated bound instead of hanging
